course: dictionary
lesson: 13803
title: Invoke: use, call on, or start
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Invoke is a formal word. It means to use something, to call on it, or to point to it. The context tells you which meaning fits: a rule, a prayer, a name, or a computer program.
explain: «She invoked the rule that lets you leave the game early.» Here invoke means she used the rule to support what she did. Swap in «used» and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The priest invoked God's help before the service.» Here it means prayed and called on God for help. «The speaker invoked her grandmother's name to make the crowd remember her kindness.» Here it means she mentioned the name so people would feel or remember something.
fact: Invoke means to use, call on, or point to something.
fact: «To invoke a law» means to use it or point to it to support what you do.
fact: «To invoke God's help» means to pray and call on God for help.
fact: «To invoke a name or idea» means to mention it so people feel or remember something.
fact: «To invoke a program» means to start it running, as in coding.
exercise: «She invoked her right to stay silent.» What does invoke mean here? | To shout loudly at someone | *To use a right to support what you do | To forget something completely | To buy a new coat
exercise: «Before the start, the choir invoked God's help.» What does invoke mean here? | To sing very loudly | To leave the church early | *To pray and call on God for help | To count the people in the seats
exercise: «Ben invoked the game by double-clicking its icon.» What does invoke mean here? | To delete the game forever | *To start the game running | To paint the screen red | To write a review of the game
test: «The coach invoked the team's motto to cheer everyone up.» What does invoke mean here? | To lose the motto | *To mention the motto so people feel brave | To write a new song | To hide the motto in a locker
test: Which meaning fits «invoke a function» in coding? | To pray for help | To mention a name | *To start it running | To break it
exam: «The lawyer invoked the rule to protect her client.» What does invoke mean here? | *To use a rule to support what you do | To break the rule on purpose | To forget the rule | To print the rule on a poster
